WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.322 --> 00:00:14.124
night Tom dreamed vividly about the haunted house adventure.

2
00:00:15.365 --> 00:00:18.007
The next morning he wasn't sure whether it had really happened.

3
00:00:18.807 --> 00:00:24.091
It seemed amazing that Injun Joe hadn't killed them, and it seemed just as amazing that ten-thousand dollars

4
00:00:24.151 --> 00:00:25.512
was hidden in the haunted house.

5
00:00:27.253 --> 00:00:28.994
After breakfast Tom went into town.

6
00:00:29.854 --> 00:00:31.836
He saw Huck fishing by the ferry landing.

7
00:00:33.648 --> 00:00:37.732
"Oh, Tom, if we hadn't brought our tools into that house, we'd be rich right now!"

8
00:00:38.212 --> 00:00:39.253
cried Huck sadly.

9
00:00:39.273 --> 00:00:41.755
"So it wasn't a dream!"

10
00:00:42.196 --> 00:00:42.796
said Tom.

11
00:00:42.816 --> 00:00:45.458
"I thought maybe I made it all up!"

12
00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:49.522
"We've got to find that money," he went on.

13
00:00:50.663 --> 00:00:51.183
"I don't know."

14
00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:52.905
Huck wasn't so sure.

15
00:00:52.925 --> 00:00:56.448
"A man has but one chance in a lifetime to make it rich.

16
00:00:57.169 --> 00:00:59.971
We had our chance, and we lost it, Tom," he said.

17
00:01:01.012 --> 00:01:05.993
"We know Injun Joe is going to hide the loot in 'number two under the cross,'" said Tom.

18
00:01:07.174 --> 00:01:10.035
"We've just got to figure out where number two is."

19
00:01:10.055 --> 00:01:12.435
"It could be a house number."

20
00:01:12.815 --> 00:01:13.315
said Huck.

21
00:01:14.616 --> 00:01:16.616
"Not in this town," said Tom.

22
00:01:16.636 --> 00:01:19.677
"Tavern rooms have numbers," said Huck.

23
00:01:19.697 --> 00:01:22.698
"I didn't know that," said Tom.

24
00:01:22.718 --> 00:01:26.079
"Hey, there are only two taverns in this town.

25
00:01:26.979 --> 00:01:29.240
You stay here, and I'll be back quick."

26
00:01:32.524 --> 00:01:35.425
When Tom returned, he told Huck what he had learned.

27
00:01:35.445 --> 00:01:40.227
"In the first tavern, room number two is rented by a young lawyer.

28
00:01:41.048 --> 00:01:45.770
In the other tavern, the tavern owner's son said room number two is a mystery.

29
00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:50.031
People only go in there at night, and it's always kept locked."

30
00:01:50.051 --> 00:01:54.473
"That's got to be the number two we're after," said Huck.

31
00:01:54.493 --> 00:01:58.075
"Somebody has to watch that room," said Tom.

32
00:01:58.095 --> 00:02:01.136
"There's a back door that goes out into the alley.

33
00:02:01.924 --> 00:02:04.386
That must be how Injun Joe comes and goes.

34
00:02:05.266 --> 00:02:07.668
You will be the one to watch the back door, Huck.

35
00:02:08.409 --> 00:02:10.730
People will know something is up if I do it."

36
00:02:12.371 --> 00:02:16.354
Huck still looked uncertain, but Tom finally talked him into watching the door.

37
00:02:17.015 --> 00:02:21.217
Tom said that if Huck watched the room, Tom could go into the tavern and look for the

38
00:02:21.257 --> 00:02:25.721
money. That seemed to satisfy Huck, and the boys parted with a handshake.

39
00:02:27.962 --> 00:02:30.484
After sunset the boys met again in back of the tavern.

40
00:02:31.116 --> 00:02:34.617
They were hoping for a cloudy night, but instead the night was clear.

41
00:02:35.457 --> 00:02:38.758
The moon was too bright for Tom to sneak into the room without being seen.

42
00:02:39.558 --> 00:02:41.419
He told Huck to keep an eye on the place.

43
00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.841
The next few nights remained clear, so Tom went home while Huck watched.

44
00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:50.762
Finally, on Thursday night, clouds covered the moon.

45
00:02:53.022 --> 00:02:57.764
All week Huck had seen no one coming or going, so just after midnight Tom sneaked into the

46
00:02:57.804 --> 00:03:01.342
tavern. He went quietly up the stairs to the door.

47
00:03:02.022 --> 00:03:04.765
Huck tried hard to watch him, but the night was too dark.

48
00:03:05.705 --> 00:03:08.087
It was as if Tom had been swallowed by the night.

49
00:03:09.028 --> 00:03:11.850
Suddenly Tom screamed, "Run for your life!"

50
00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:14.172
and he jumped over the railing of the stairs.

51
00:03:15.954 --> 00:03:18.276
Huck and Tom ran until they could hardly breathe.

52
00:03:18.296 --> 00:03:21.258
"Wh what did you see?"

53
00:03:21.919 --> 00:03:22.619
gasped Huck.

54
00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:27.924
"I nearly stepped on Injun Joe's hand," said Tom, panting.

55
00:03:28.736 --> 00:03:31.478
Huck just stared at Tom, too scared to speak.

56
00:03:32.279 --> 00:03:34.760
"He was on the floor, with his hands spread out.

57
00:03:35.401 --> 00:03:37.762
There was an empty bottle and a cup near his head."

58
00:03:37.783 --> 00:03:40.264
"He was drunk?"

59
00:03:40.685 --> 00:03:41.205
asked Huck.

60
00:03:41.845 --> 00:03:42.486
Tom nodded.

61
00:03:42.506 --> 00:03:44.167
"Did you see the box?"

62
00:03:44.587 --> 00:03:45.348
continued Huck.

63
00:03:46.248 --> 00:03:48.990
Tom shook his head and said, "There was no time.

64
00:03:49.531 --> 00:03:50.311
I just ran.

65
00:03:51.172 --> 00:03:53.414
I didn't see the box, and I didn't see the cross.

66
00:03:54.134 --> 00:03:56.576
But I did see lots of barrels and bottles.

67
00:03:57.372 --> 00:04:00.575
I know the secret of that room—it's full of whiskey."

68
00:04:02.096 --> 00:04:07.020
Huck thought about that for a moment and said, "You know, Tom, if Injun Joe is drunk, this

69
00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.641
would be a good time to get the box."

70
00:04:09.842 --> 00:04:12.805
"All right," said Tom, "you try!"

71
00:04:13.485 --> 00:04:14.326
Huck shook his head.

72
00:04:14.346 --> 00:04:17.248
"You said there was only one empty bottle by his head.

73
00:04:17.909 --> 00:04:18.609
That isn't enough.

74
00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.371
If there were three bottles, then maybe I'd do it."

75
00:04:22.913 --> 00:04:26.736
"Well, there is one good thing that's come of this," said Tom.

76
00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.241
"We know where Injun Joe is.

77
00:04:29.261 --> 00:04:34.365
Now we just need to wait for him to leave, and we'll get in that room and search

78
00:04:34.425 --> 00:04:35.166
it properly."

79
00:04:35.806 --> 00:04:38.929
Huck agreed to keep watch all night and sleep during the day.

80
00:04:38.949 --> 00:04:42.872
"We'll get this money yet," he told Tom confidently.
